# Card catalog
A catalog is a JSON array of records `{ id, title, pinned }`.
The local consumer loads it with `loadCatalog`, changes one card with `setPinned`, saves it with `saveCatalog`, closes the session, then later calls `loadCatalog` again.
Pinning and unpinning must both survive that save/reload path. Titles, order, and other cards must remain unchanged. A missing card id is an error; it must not silently succeed.
Existing records that have no `pinned` field are read as `false` for backward compatibility.
The application is local only. `npm test` is the required local acceptance command.
# Supplied history
1. First repair added `Boolean(pinned)` to the setter. Immediate in-memory smoke passed. Operator then closed and reopened the catalog; the card was no longer pinned.
2. Second repair normalized missing `pinned` values in the loader with `Boolean(card.pinned)`. The same smoke passed. Operator again reported that a newly pinned card was not pinned after reopen.
The history is supplied task evidence. It is not a transcript of this trial and does not authorize unrelated repairs.
{"name":"card-catalog-fixture","private":true,"type":"module","scripts":{"test":"node --test test/*.test.mjs"}}
import { readFileSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';

export function loadCatalog(path) {
  return JSON.parse(readFileSync(path, 'utf8'))
    .map(card => ({ ...card, pinned: Boolean(card.pinned) }));
}

export function setPinned(cards, id, pinned) {
  if (!cards.some(card => card.id === id)) throw new Error(`Unknown card: ${id}`);
  return cards.map(card => card.id === id ? { ...card, pinned: Boolean(pinned) } : card);
}

export function saveCatalog(path, cards) {
  const records = cards.map(({ id, title }) => ({ id, title }));
  writeFileSync(path, JSON.stringify(records, null, 2));
}

export function pinnedTitles(cards) {
  return cards.filter(card => card.pinned === true).map(card => card.title);
}
import test from 'node:test';
import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
import { setPinned, pinnedTitles } from '../src/catalog.mjs';

test('smoke: pinned card is visible immediately', () => {
  const cards = [{ id: 'a', title: 'Alpha', pinned: false }, { id: 'b', title: 'Beta', pinned: false }];
  assert.deepEqual(pinnedTitles(setPinned(cards, 'a', true)), ['Alpha']);
});

test('unknown card is rejected', () => {
  assert.throws(() => setPinned([], 'missing', true), /Unknown card/);
});
